= August Thalheimer

Thalheimer is the party's leading theorist and a close ally of Brandler. He sees the crisis as a long struggle whose outcome depends on how many workers the party can win, not on a single decisive day. His opponents call this cowardice dressed up as theory; on the evidence so far, the question is open.

